{
  "slug": "BELONGS_TO_ACCOUNT__aws_core",
  "name": "Belongs To Account",
  "description": "A resource is owned by an AWS account (resource -> account): the account a collector reads from the item's owner field (OwnerId, OwnerAccountId, ownerAccount) or, where the item has none, the account the resource was collected from. One relationship, ownership, over every account-owned aws_core type; the sources are listed so a new type is added on purpose. A reference, not containment: a resource shared through AWS RAM is used from other accounts, and an account's subtree can exceed the cascade cap. The `_TO` is the locative preposition of 'belongs to'. Excluded: region, availability zone, account, the Organizations types (their placement is NESTED_UNDER_PARENT) and Bedrock foundation models, which AWS owns.",
